---
import UnfoldLayout from '../../layouts/UnfoldLayout.astro';
---

<UnfoldLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Unfold"
  description="How the Unfold app handles data: screen snapshots stay in memory, crash reports without personal data, no account, no tracking."
>
  <main class="container mx-auto px-6 pt-10 pb-24 max-w-4xl text-slate-800">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-8">PRIVACY POLICY</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-slate-500 font-medium">Last updated: 2026-10-22</p>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-lg">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how the Android app Unfold (package <code>com.cmart.unfold</code>, “Unfold”, “we”,
        “us”) handles data. In short: Unfold has no account and no own server. Screen content never leaves your phone.
        The only data we receive are crash and error reports without personal data.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">1. Controller / Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Controller: Christoph Martin<br />
        Address: Fischerweg 8, 7503 Großpetersdorf, Austria<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:info@endure-cycling.com" class="text-accent hover:underline">info@endure-cycling.com</a>
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">2. Accessibility service and screen content</h2>
      <p>
        Unfold uses an Android accessibility service to draw the fold transition on top of the screen when you open or
        close your phone. This is the only purpose of the service. It does not help users with disabilities and is not
        declared as an accessibility tool.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>
          When a transition starts, the service takes a snapshot of the current screen and folds it. The snapshot exists
          only in memory for the length of that one transition (about half a second). It is never saved, logged,
          analysed or sent anywhere.
        </li>
        <li>On the lock screen and for apps that block screenshots, no snapshot is taken; the effect runs on a neutral surface instead.</li>
        <li>
          The service does not read text, does not record what you type, does not record which apps you use and does not
          perform actions on your behalf. It only looks up the position of the top window so the snapshot covers the
          right area.
        </li>
        <li>You enable the service yourself in the Android settings after Unfold explains what it does, and you can turn it off there at any time.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">3. Data stored on your phone</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>Your settings (effect on/off, direction, fine-tuning, device profile) and onboarding progress</li>
        <li>The start date of your 14-day trial</li>
        <li>Whether you own the Lifetime Unlock (a cache of what Google Play reports)</li>
        <li>Hinge sensor and display measurements for your phone model</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These data stay on the device. If Android backup is enabled on your phone, Google may include the settings,
        the trial start and the purchase cache in your device backup under Google's terms; device-specific measurements
        are excluded.
      </p>
      <p>
        The trial start date is also saved in Google Play services Block Store, so that a reinstall does not restart the
        trial. Block Store keeps this single date on your Google account's device backup, end-to-end encrypted where
        your device supports it. It is not linked to your identity by us, and we cannot read it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">4. Crash and error reports (Sentry)</h2>
      <p>
        When Unfold crashes, freezes (ANR) or hits an error, it sends a report to Sentry (Functional Software, Inc.,
        USA) so we can fix the problem. A report contains:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>Stack trace and error message</li>
        <li>App version, Android version, device maker and model, hinge sensor type</li>
        <li>A random installation ID and session health (whether a session ended in a crash)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Reports never contain screenshots, screen content, session replays, the names of apps you use, your name, email
        address or any other personal data; Unfold removes such fields before sending. Like any server, Sentry sees the
        IP address of the connection that delivers a report.
        Legal basis: our legitimate interest in a working app (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)). Reports are kept for up to 90 days.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">5. Purchases (Google Play)</h2>
      <p>
        The Lifetime Unlock is sold through Google Play Billing. Google processes the payment as an independent
        controller under its own privacy policy. Unfold only receives from Google Play whether you own the product and
        the purchase confirmation needed to unlock it. We do not receive your name, email address or payment details.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">6. Notifications</h2>
      <p>
        If you allow notifications, Unfold reminds you two days before and on the day your trial ends. The reminders
        are scheduled on the phone; no push service or server is involved.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">7. What we do not do</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>No account, no login, no own server</li>
        <li>No analytics, no advertising, no tracking SDKs</li>
        <li>No sale or sharing of data with third parties for their own purposes</li>
        <li>No collection of location, contacts, photos, messages or other personal content</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">8. International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Sentry may process crash reports in the United States. Where required, we rely on the EU Standard Contractual
        Clauses and Sentry's data processing agreement.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">9. Your rights (EEA/UK/Switzerland)</h2>
      <p>
        You have the right to access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability, and the right
        to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority (in Austria: Datenschutzbehörde, dsb.gv.at). Because crash
        reports carry no personal identifiers, we usually cannot link a report to you; tell us your device model and the
        approximate time of a crash and we will search for it. Contact:
        <a href="mailto:info@endure-cycling.com" class="text-accent hover:underline">info@endure-cycling.com</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Deleting data: uninstalling Unfold removes all data stored on the phone. To also remove the trial date from
        Block Store, clear Unfold's data in the Android settings before uninstalling, or remove the app's backup in your
        Google account. Crash reports expire automatically after 90 days, or earlier on request.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">10. This website</h2>
      <p>
        The Unfold pages on endure-cycling.com set no cookies and load no analytics. The site is hosted on GitHub Pages
        (GitHub, Inc., USA), which processes your IP address to deliver the pages.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">11. Children</h2>
      <p>Unfold is not directed at children under 13 and collects no personal data from anyone.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6">12. Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this Privacy Policy. The “Last updated” date above shows the current version.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</UnfoldLayout>
